This course covers the basic neuroanatomical and neurophysiological underpinnings of neural systems (e.g. vision), psychological processes (e.g. memory) and behaviour (e.g. sleep), focusing on the organization and functioning of the nervous system. This course will also cover the basic mechanisms of neuropathology and neuroplasticity. Prerequisite(s): PSYC 1013 or PSYC 1113.', 'PSYC', 3, 0, 2, '[{"codes":["PSYC-1013","OR","PSYC-1113"],"textExtension":"- Must be completed prior to taking this course."}]');

