2026 Fall NURS-4703-FA01 Special Topics 1

Advanced Nursing Care in Adult Critical Illness This asynchronous course prepares registered nurses to care for critically ill adults using a concept-based, evidence-informed approach. Learners apply pathophysiology, assessment, and clinical judgement to high-acuity scenarios integrating perfusion, gas exchange, neurologic status, infection, and emergencies. Interactive modules, virtual case studies, and threaded discussions emphasize person-centred care, interprofessional communication, ethics, and resilience in contemporary critical care practice for nurses.

Professor for the course will be: Tori Dawson, RN, BScN MScN

 2027 Winter NURS-4703-WI01

Transitioning to Nursing Practice  This course prepares students for the transition from student nurse to registered nurse. This course emphasizes core nursing competencies including professional identity, communication, prioritization, leadership, cultural safety, and navigating workplace systems including experiences of racism and discrimination. Students will examine challenges of transitioning to practice, along with exploring strategies for success through reflective and evidence-informed learning.

Professor will be: Maddie Gallant RN PhD', 'NURS', 3, 0, 4, '[]');

